CONVERSATION:
bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: How do we publish the Snashots?
Hi 3f21e54c5c5ffd50fe3680acc025bb1d. I think tomorrow is the last publication day until May 24.
Were we planning to pub..." | raw="
CONVERSATION:
bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: How do we publish the Snashots?
Hi 3f21e54c5c5ffd50fe3680acc025bb1d. I think tomorrow is the last publication day until May 24.
Were we planning to publish both snapshots?
yes
Hmm, already too late for this week. Next opportunity is May 24.
What!
:(
requests for tomorrow were due last Friday.
http://lists.w3.org/Archives/Member/w3c-css-wg/2011AprJun/0275.html
I guess sending in that email last Wednesday was to late, then
://
Sorry, I didn't think about the AC publication stop,
So what do we have to do to get these published on May 24th?
Send in a request. :-)  We can send the request now.
Yeah, but don't we have to do something to the status section?
it's not a WD
Yes, but I'll have to check the pubrules for what is special about Notes.
Probably not much, though.
-&gt; http://services.w3.org/xslt?xmlfile=http%3A%2F%2Fservices.w3.org%2Ftidy%2Ftidy%3FpassThroughXHTML%3D1%26docAddr%3Dhttp%253A%252F%252Fdev.w3.org%252Fcsswg%252Fcss-2007%252F&amp;xslfile=http%3A%2F%2Fservices.w3.org%2Fxslt%3Fxmlfile%3Dhttp%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2005%2F07%2Fpubrules%253Fuimode%253Dchecker_full%2526year%253D0001%2526docstatus%253Dwg-note-tr%2526rectrack%253Dyes%2526prevrec%253Dnone%2526patpol%253Dw3c%2526normative%253Dyes%2526uri%253Dhttp%25253A%25252F%252
Hmm, did that work?
nope
tries
It has the boilerplate text:
Publication as a Working Group Note does not imply endorsement by the W3C Membership. This is a draft document and may be updated, replaced or obsoleted by other documents at any time. It is inappropriate to cite this document as other than work in progress.
Which isn't all that different from a WD.
um
but is it a draft?
we published a couple WDs already
is there an LC process for notes or something?
A Note is by definition not stable. But we are expected to add in our own words what we really mean by publishing a Note.
No, no LC for notes.
So
You can't ever cite a Note as anything other than a work in progress
?
Correct
But a REC, which in many cases is more likely to change in response to errata,
is not a work in progress
?
Notes can means many things: a first draft when it is not yet certain it will become a WD, a temporary stop in development, a definitive stop in development (when the WG ceases to exist, e.g.), or just something interesting that the WG wants to publish...
hm, ok
doesn't think it makes sense to mark this as unstable, personally but can't argue with pubrules, can we
maybe we should just leave it as a WD indefinitely...
since that has roughly the same status message anyway :)
