CONVERSATION:
Looking into the license for existing-rel-values
Three authors made changes to that page before 2007-12-29.
tantek and andy mabbett both have PD declarations on their author pages
the third author, Makacow, doesn't have a user page
so the content by makacow isn't PD
it was a small change and that content is still on the page (he or she spotted rel=details being used in the wild)
were we to remove the mention of rel=details, we could add the cc-pd-license template to the page
good morning
the cc-pd-license is only applicable to User: pages as it is written
do you have the diff URL of Makacow's change(s) to rel-license?
http://microformats.org/wiki/index.php?title=existing-rel-values&amp;diff=22188&amp;oldid=22045
re: the template being applicable only to user pages, that doesn't match our established copyright practice:
&quot;As more contributors add a public domain declaration to their user pages, and more non-public-domain content is removed, more pages fully enter the public domain. After reviewing such pages, the microformats admins will add the http://microformats.org/wiki/Template:cc-pd-license template to them to explicitly indicate that all content of the page is in the public domain.&quot;
-- http://microformats.org/wiki/Microformats_Wiki:Copyrights
it's worth mentioning that the WHATWG RelExtensions page also mentions rel=details
oh right
but doesn't attribute the proposal to anywhere
http://wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/RelExtensions
sorry I had the &quot;declaration&quot; and &quot;license&quot; mixed up
*nod*
the only use of rel=details in the wild that I'm able to find by googling is on w3.org
well this is particularly easy, I just checked w3.org and w3.org's News page, and there is no presence of rel=&quot;details&quot; so I'm simply going to remove (undo) Makacow's edit in its entirety as it doesn't add any real world information.
yeah, actually, now that i've clicked through, it's in plain text
e.g. http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/Europe/200207/rsscal/xslt-rss-events.html
if someone finds it in the future, they can always add it and cite a precise URL
right
cool
yeah, the circa-2002 w3.org markup guidelines call for using rel=details: http://www.w3.org/2002/10/scrape/WG-Style-Guidelines.html
but those guidelines don't appear to be used anymore
I'll remove the mention from the WHATWG RelExtensions page
edit made to existing-rel-values page accordingly: http://microformats.org/wiki/index.php?title=existing-rel-values&amp;diff=43360&amp;oldid=43300
cool. can you add the cc-pd-license template too?
fd9ef1223e855714294498ebfde79f98 - since you did the checking of the history to verify no other non-PD edits, you should add the template
btw re: that w3.org home page markup guidelines  - probably worth adding this to a brainstorming section somewhere: http://www.w3.org/2002/10/scrape/WG-Style-Guidelines.html#apc1
ok, will do
while we're looking at the wiki, how do I go about deleting a (spam) page?
I was just about to do some of that
I think you need to be a wiki admin to do that
makes sense
ah there is wikimedia terminology here
SysOps
and Bureaucrats
spam removed and spammers blocked
well, if you feel generous with the lowest-power setting that lets me clean up spam, I'll happily do so when I notice it, like I do on the whatwg wiki
I would be happy to propose that to the other admins
incidentally, the existing-rel-values page has never been spammed.
that is interesting
(which I'll be pointing out in my CP to make HTML5 reference it for rel values)
I'm sure it will be eventually :)
indeed
fd9ef1223e855714294498ebfde79f98, just to be sure I have this right, you're volunteering to help out as a wiki-only admin e.g. as noted here: http://microformats.org/wiki/admins#Wiki-only_admins
fd9ef1223e855714294498ebfde79f98, just to be sure I have this right, you're volunteering to help out as a wiki-only admin e.g. as noted here: http://microformats.org/wiki/admins#Wiki-only_admins
